  "body": "What changed\r\n- `feature_click::ask`: plain/Ctrl edge click uses `EdgeUnit::Run`; only Shift (without Ctrl) uses `Chain`. Cause of the sporadic picking: the default unit was the tangent chain (up to 30 degrees), so a click took 1, 2 or a whole outline depending on geometry.\r\n- `edge_pick::toggle`: Ctrl+click on an edge already covered by a stored loop/chain pick removes it instead of stacking an overlapping pick.\r\n- New `pick_ink` module: selected picks 3 px with a dark halo, viewport hover 5 px (was 1 px lines). #1507 Geometry-row hover landed on main (371db9c7c) and is kept as is; this PR adds nothing further for it.\r\n\r\nTested\r\n- Pinning: `edge_click_modifiers::contour_click_ctrl_and_shift_pick_the_same_every_time`, `::pocket_click_ctrl_and_shift_pick_the_same_every_time` (fail on the old ask), `::hovering_a_selection_rows_remove_button_highlights_that_pick`, `pick_ink::tests::selected_and_hover_styles_are_strong_and_tell_apart`.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` 712 passed; `--test edge_loop_pick` ok; clippy -D warnings clean on camcraft-ui.\r\n\r\nNot exercised: GUI not hand-tested; screenshots owed (before/after of selected and hovered edges). Shift-hover loop preview and viewport-to-row reverse highlight not done. `cargo xtask gate quick --base main` ran irrelevant suites against a stale local main and was stopped; targeted runs above stand in.\r\n\r\nDecision: docs/decisions/1505-edge-pick-style.md\r\nChangelog: Edge picks take one edge per click (Shift = loop); selected and hovered picks drawn thicker with a halo (#1505)\r\nEffort: medium\r\n\r\nFixes #1505\r\nRefs #1507\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
